Plain and simple summary :
**Not indexed** = don’t include this webpage in search results, but it can still be crawled and visited.

*   Users won’t find this page when searching on Google.
*   Search engines won’t create an index for it.
*   It won’t compete with other pages in rankings.
*   This is used when you don’t want specific pages to appear in search results but still want to keep their functionality or link to other important pages.

The points above can really affect SEO rankings — this is actually the first time I learned this. If you’re also dealing with multilingual sites combined with regional versions, it’s worth considering how link equity influences crawlers and SEO!

